{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784148-quick-question-about-silver","id":784148,"title":"Quick Question about Silver","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Werewolf: The Forsaken"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-12-11T07:15:21-08:00","id":784148,"title":"Quick Question about Silver","content":"So again rereading stuff from the book making sure i have caught up with all the new changes between 1ed and 2ed and the Silver second jumped out at me. So apparently now even the Forsaken are burned by the touch of Silver not just the Pure. Not sure how I feel about this I liked there being a difference in how silver reacted between the two groups. But I guess it does really drive home the role Silver should have in any story.<br /> <br /> What do you all think?<br /> <br /> \u201cSilver, the metal of Luna, burns Uratha flesh like nothing<br /> else. Silver weapons always deal aggravated damage to Uratha.<br /> <b>A non-damaging touch with silver doesn\u2019t cause damage, but</b><br /> <b>causes intense pain so long as the werewolf remains in contact</b>,<br /> and leaves lasting scars as if from aggravated wounds.\u201d<br /> <br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/10059-ak_cahalith","name":"AK_Cahalith","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar10059_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T07:31:37-08:00","id":784154,"title":"","content":"Mechanically it's no different from first edition. I don't mind.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-11T08:25:03-08:00","id":784185,"title":"","content":"If you check the Prey section you'll note that Pure still suffer a far harsher reaction to touching silver than the Forsaken do.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>- Chris Allen, Aberrant Line Developer, Freelance Writer<br /> <br /> \u200bLike my work? Feel like helping me stay supplied with tea? Check out my <b><a href=\"https://www.patreon.com/acrozatarim\" target=\"_blank\">Patreon</a></b>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1757-acrozatarim","name":"Acrozatarim","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1757_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1892"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T03:48:15-08:00","id":791471,"title":"","content":"Though for added fun, it looks like silver would be a pretty common influence for artificial spirits, due to the incredibly hostile bent they've been given it seems, if the Spark Blood Seneschal is any indication as to how unfriendly they could be. After all, silver is still used in many electrical systems, platinum too, but hey, platinum doesn't burn werewolves lol.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1686-korogra","name":"Korogra","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar1686_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1310"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T10:48:46-08:00","id":791677,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Korogra</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-forsaken/784148-quick-question-about-silver?p=791471#post791471\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Though for added fun, it looks like silver would be a pretty common influence for artificial spirits, due to the incredibly hostile bent they've been given it seems, if the Spark Blood Seneschal is any indication as to how unfriendly they could be. After all, silver is still used in many electrical systems, platinum too, but hey, platinum doesn't burn werewolves lol.</div> </div> </div> </div>That hardly justifies an electronic spirit displaying influences in silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T11:23:49-08:00","id":791701,"title":"","content":"It's not just about its use as how relevant it is and I imagine most people don't place much emphasis on the silver content.<br /> <br /> Still if you wanted to do it, probably a better way than giving a computer or electrical spirit a silver influence would be to make them part of an umia that has lesser silver wire spirits they can boss around for defensive purposes. If they are particularly warlike they might divvy out a portion of their Essence to keep the otherwise starved spirit from dormancy.<br /> <br /> As an added benefit this means that you can incorporate silver without it being an automatic death sentence for werewolves. Spirits of rank 3 or higher can already do enough Lethal damage to knock a werewolf into aggravated as is. But having it around Rank 1 or 2 spirits gives you some worrisome 'meat' shields without the practical guarantee of death. I'd still be be reluctant to use Rank 2 spirits, though, I <i>really </i>don't think the silver is really relevant enough in your average electrical system to warrant spirits of any real strength, plus rank 2 spirits are still capable of doing 7 or higher damage in one shot without too much effort.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/886-nofather","name":"nofather","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar886_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"11016"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-23T13:34:31-08:00","id":791768,"title":"","content":"Giving influence: silver to some electronics spirits just because they got some components made out of it would be like giving car spirits influence: metal for the same reason.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/576-ephsy","name":"Ephsy","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar576_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2615"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-12-26T01:28:17-08:00","id":793023,"title":"","content":"I agree that most electronic spirits shouldn't have influence Silver. Maybe it would be more justified for an RFID spirit since silver is the main component of their design rather than being incidental. However as Ephsy says that's not the logic we use with most other spirits, so it would be a bit strange.<br /> <br /> If you really want an electronic spirit with Influence: Silver, how about this?<br /> <br /> <i>The police station decides to scrap the server that was used for storing video evidence for the Violent Crimes taskforce. Hundreds of hours of video-footage or pain and suffering, combined with the anger and drive for justice of the police accessing it had stirred the dreams of this spirit. So much emotional energy was focused on it that when its physical host was destroyed it didn't allow itself to fade away, it woke up hungry for more Essence. Due to budget cuts though the police were desperate to save money wherever they could and so they sold their electronic scrap to a company that recycled electronic components for silver. <br /> <br /> The spirit woke up in this facility, watching other electronic spirits fading away as one by one their physical forms were trashed and recycled. It hunted and devoured them. Most weren't even good for a single mote of essence, still asleep and barely holding onto existence. A few though had been touched by strong emotions like it had and that recharged the spirit. Over time it changed from the spirit of a Computer, incorporating spirits of mobile phones, televisions and the circuits of every sort of device imaginable. Its identity began to blur until it was a mere electronics spirit and it was able to rest once again inside the machines of the facility, broad enough in portfolio now to regain essence merely from its environment. It ripped apart spirit and machine alike, to fashion silver on its production line.<br /> <br /> Even then all would have been fine if a member of the Pure tribes, a fire touched zealot, hadn't learned of this spirit's existence and decided to turn it again the Uratha. He began binding spirits into electronic devices and sending them off to be recycled at this company. Every spirit was devoured by the new spirit that claimed the silver recycling depot. Every single spirit bound in was a spirit of Justice. It stirred the long lost memories of its very first incarnation, the emotional energy that the police had poured into it. Because of these memories the spirit could absorb these bound spirits of justice, even though they were incompatible essences. Over time this quickly mutated the spirit into a Magath, combining the natures of electronics, justice and just as planned by the Pure... silver.<br /> <br /> At night the pure zealot went into the presence of the Magath and explained that a great crime had been committed. The Uratha had murdered their father, the great Wolf Spirit Urfafah. He performed Chiminage to the spirit and prayed for justice against the Forsaken tribes. Now the spirit goes forth every night of the new moon to punish the Uratha for their sins, the new moon to ensure that Luna doesn't need to see justice done to her children for the murder of her husband.</i><br /> <br /> That would be a great adversary for a VERY experienced pack of Uratha. A dangerous foe and if they pursue it to its lair, it lives in a building completely full of recycled silver.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6748-michael-kenner","name":"Michael Kenner","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6748_2.png","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"380"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}